+### How to actually give the vision model a picture — read this, it is not obvious
+
+**A screenshot reaches a model only as a CLI `--file` attachment. The `task` tool that
+spawns a subagent carries text only.** So you **cannot** get a visual review by
+spawning `hm-reviewer-visual` as a subagent — it would receive no image and would
+correctly answer `UNVERIFIED_VISUAL`, and the whole of R3 would be lost.
+
+Call it **directly**, from the shell, one command per batch of images:
+
+```
+opencode run "<your review instructions>" --agent hm-reviewer-visual --auto --dir <repo> --file <image1.png> --file <image2.png>
+```
+
+`hm-reviewer-visual` is `mode: all`, so this works. The equivalent through the dynamic
+runner also works and takes a prompt file:
+
+```
+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\tools\hm-orchestrator\run-model.ps1 -Model deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp -PromptFile <prompt.txt> -File <image1.png>,<image2.png>
+```
