+### R13 — Confirm the harness repair, and report it
+
+Claude found and fixed a defect in the orchestration harness itself on 2026-09-12. It
+had to be fixed before this mission could start, because **no OpenCode agent could run
+at all**.
+
+**What was wrong.** All 11 files in `.opencode/agents/` declared a key called
+`permissions:` (plural) holding a list of `{action, resource, effect}` rules. That key
+does not exist in OpenCode's configuration schema. The real key is `permission`
+(singular) and it is an **object keyed by tool name** whose values are
+`allow` / `deny` / `ask`, or a pattern-to-action map. Two files in
+`.opencode/commands/` had the same class of mistake: `subagent:` where the schema says
+`subtask:`.
+
+**Why it broke everything.** An unrecognised frontmatter key is not ignored — OpenCode
+forwards it to the model provider as a request option. The OpenCode Go gateway now
+rejects unknown fields, so every run died instantly with:
+
+```
+Error from provider (Console Go): Upstream request failed:
+[invalid_request_error] invalid request body: json: unknown field "permissions"
+```
+
+**The quieter, worse half of the same bug.** Because the key was never recognised,
+**none of those permission rules had ever been enforced.** Every agent had been running
+on OpenCode's defaults. The guard rails in those files — never read `.env`, never
+`git push`, never edit `CLAUDE.md`, only these subagents — existed on paper only. This
+is the codebase's classic failure: two vocabularies for one concept, and the one
+actually in force was not the one anybody had written down. It also explains the
+previous run's note that "the tool refuses to delete files here" — that refusal came
+from somewhere other than the policy everyone believed was running.
+
+**A third defect, found by testing rather than reading.** `hm-reviewer-visual` was
+`mode: subagent`. A screenshot reaches a model only as a CLI `--file` attachment, and
+the `task` tool that spawns a subagent carries text only. So the vision reviewer, the
+one agent whose entire job is looking at pictures, **could never have received a
+picture**. It is now `mode: all`.
+
+**What you must do for R13.** Do not re-fix it. Confirm it and record it:
+
+1. Confirm every file in `.opencode/agents/` and `.opencode/commands/` uses only
+   schema-valid frontmatter keys, and that each one's YAML parses.
+2. Confirm from your own run that the permission rules are now in force — for example,
+   note that the supervisor could not edit a product file and had to delegate it.
+3. Record in the report, in plain words, that the guard rails were **not** active
+   before today and are active now.
+
+**You may not edit `.opencode/*` yourself** — the worker permissions deny it, on
+purpose. If you believe a further change is needed there, escalate with the exact file
+and the exact reason.
